# Git: commit and push after changes

Whenever you modify, create, or delete tracked source or config files in this repository (not `node_modules`), immediately afterward run:

1. `git add` for the files you changed (never stage `node_modules` unless the user explicitly asks).
2. `git commit -m "<short imperative description of what changed>"`
3. `git push`

Do this in the same turn as the edits unless the user forbids git operations or authentication will fail (then say so and stop).
